§ `Regulation 21: is the person entitled to the up-rating increase?`

-- (5): the general case: entitled to a state pension and an overseas resident immediately before the increase.
#ASSERT `regulation 21: whether the person is entitled to the up-rating increase` `not deferred, entitled and overseas` EQUALS `the person is not entitled to the up-rating increase under regulation 21`
#ASSERT `regulation 21: whether the person is entitled to the up-rating increase` `not deferred, entitled but not overseas` EQUALS `regulation 21 does not take the up-rating increase away`
#ASSERT `regulation 21: whether the person is entitled to the up-rating increase` `not deferred, overseas but not entitled` EQUALS `regulation 21 does not take the up-rating increase away`
-- (2)(a): regulation 21 bites on an increase only if regulations say it applies to that increase.
#ASSERT `regulation 21: whether the person is entitled to the up-rating increase` `regulations not made, entitled and overseas` EQUALS `regulation 21 does not apply to this up-rating increase`
-- (3), (4)(a): an increase in respect of the deferral period, for a person overseas throughout.
#ASSERT `regulation 21(3): paragraph (4) applies` `deferred 2025, ended entitled and overseas; increase in the deferral, overseas throughout`
#ASSERT `regulation 21: whether the person is entitled to the up-rating increase` `deferred 2025, ended entitled and overseas; increase in the deferral, overseas throughout` EQUALS `the person is not entitled to the up-rating increase under regulation 21`
#ASSERT `regulation 21: whether the person is entitled to the up-rating increase` `deferred 2025, ended entitled and overseas; increase in the deferral, not overseas throughout` EQUALS `regulation 21 does not take the up-rating increase away`
-- The first and last days of the deferral period are in it.
#ASSERT `regulation 21: whether the person is entitled to the up-rating increase` `deferred 2025, ended entitled and overseas; increase on the first day of the deferral` EQUALS `the person is not entitled to the up-rating increase under regulation 21`
#ASSERT `regulation 21: whether the person is entitled to the up-rating increase` `deferred 2025, ended entitled and overseas; increase on the last day of the deferral` EQUALS `the person is not entitled to the up-rating increase under regulation 21`
-- (4)(b): after the deferral, overseas at the time of the increase.
#ASSERT `regulation 21: whether the person is entitled to the up-rating increase` `deferred 2025, ended entitled and overseas; increase the day after the deferral, overseas` EQUALS `the person is not entitled to the up-rating increase under regulation 21`
#ASSERT `regulation 21: whether the person is entitled to the up-rating increase` `deferred 2025, ended entitled and overseas; increase after the deferral, not overseas then` EQUALS `regulation 21 does not take the up-rating increase away`
-- An increase before the deferral began is in neither (a) nor (b); and (5) is for the "other cases". Nothing takes it away.
#ASSERT `regulation 21: whether the person is entitled to the up-rating increase` `deferred 2025, ended entitled and overseas; increase before the deferral began` EQUALS `regulation 21 does not take the up-rating increase away`
-- (3) needs entitlement and overseas residence when the deferral ended; otherwise it is an "other case" under (5).
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 21(3): paragraph (4) applies` `deferred 2025, ended not overseas, but overseas and entitled at an increase in 2027`)
#ASSERT `regulation 21: whether the person is entitled to the up-rating increase` `deferred 2025, ended not overseas, but overseas and entitled at an increase in 2027` EQUALS `the person is not entitled to the up-rating increase under regulation 21`
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 21(3): paragraph (4) applies` `deferred 2025, ended overseas but not entitled; overseas at an increase in 2027`)
#ASSERT `regulation 21: whether the person is entitled to the up-rating increase` `deferred 2025, ended overseas but not entitled; overseas at an increase in 2027` EQUALS `regulation 21 does not take the up-rating increase away`

§ `Regulation 21(6): the specified territory`

#ASSERT `regulation 21(6): the place is a territory specified for sections 18(4) and 20(2) and (3) of the 2014 Act` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 21(6): the place is a territory specified for sections 18(4) and 20(2) and (3) of the 2014 Act` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 21(6): the place is a territory specified for sections 18(4) and 20(2) and (3) of the 2014 Act` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 21(6): the place is a territory specified for sections 18(4) and 20(2) and (3) of the 2014 Act` FALSE TRUE)

§ `Regulation 22: the rate on which the increment is worked`

`part: overseas, outside Great Britain and specified territories` MEANS PartOfDeferral WITH
    `the person was an overseas resident during the part` IS TRUE
    `the person was in Great Britain or a territory specified in regulation 21(6) during the part` IS FALSE

`part: not an overseas resident` MEANS PartOfDeferral WITH
    `the person was an overseas resident during the part` IS FALSE
    `the person was in Great Britain or a territory specified in regulation 21(6) during the part` IS TRUE

`part: overseas resident but in Great Britain or a specified territory` MEANS PartOfDeferral WITH
    `the person was an overseas resident during the part` IS TRUE
    `the person was in Great Britain or a territory specified in regulation 21(6) during the part` IS TRUE

-- (1): applies where the person was an overseas resident for any part of the deferral period.
#ASSERT `regulation 22(1): regulation 22 applies` (LIST `part: not an overseas resident`, `part: overseas, outside Great Britain and specified territories`)
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 22(1): regulation 22 applies` (LIST `part: not an overseas resident`))
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 22(1): regulation 22 applies` EMPTY)
-- (2): overseas and not in Great Britain or a specified territory: the rate just before the START of the part.
#ASSERT `regulation 22(2) and (3): the rate on which the increment for the part is worked` `part: overseas, outside Great Britain and specified territories` EQUALS `the weekly rate immediately before the start of that part of the deferral period`
-- (3): not an overseas resident: the rate just before the END of the part.
#ASSERT `regulation 22(2) and (3): the rate on which the increment for the part is worked` `part: not an overseas resident` EQUALS `the weekly rate immediately before the end of that part of the deferral period`
-- Overseas but in Great Britain or a specified territory: neither paragraph says (fork F27). Asserted.
#ASSERT `regulation 22(2) and (3): the rate on which the increment for the part is worked` `part: overseas resident but in Great Britain or a specified territory` EQUALS `regulation 22 gives no reference rate for this part`
-- The increment: 1/9 of 1% (1/900) times the weeks times the chosen rate.
-- 10 weeks, rate 900 at the start of the part and 450 at the end: 10 against the start rate, 5 against the end rate.
#ASSERT `regulation 22: the increment for the part` `part: overseas, outside Great Britain and specified territories` 10 900 450 EQUALS JUST 10
#ASSERT `regulation 22: the increment for the part` `part: not an overseas resident` 10 900 450 EQUALS JUST 5
#ASSERT `regulation 22: the increment for the part` `part: overseas resident but in Great Britain or a specified territory` 10 900 450 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Regulation 23: where regulations 12A and 22 both apply`

`the deferral of 2027, for regulation 23` MEANS DeferralPeriod WITH
    `first day of the deferral` IS YMD 2027 1 1
    `last day of the deferral` IS YMD 2027 12 31

-- (1): both apply: a non-uprating change inside the deferral period and an overseas part.
#ASSERT `regulation 23(1): regulations 12A and 22 both apply` `the deferral of 2027, for regulation 23` (LIST YMD 2027 3 1) (LIST `part: overseas, outside Great Britain and specified territories`)
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 23(1): regulations 12A and 22 both apply` `the deferral of 2027, for regulation 23` EMPTY (LIST `part: overseas, outside Great Britain and specified territories`))
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 23(1): regulations 12A and 22 both apply` `the deferral of 2027, for regulation 23` (LIST YMD 2027 3 1) (LIST `part: not an overseas resident`))
-- (4): the rate that stands in for regulation 12A(2)'s weekly rate: regulation 22(2) or (3).
#ASSERT `regulation 23(4): the rate that stands in place of the weekly rate in regulation 12A(2)` `part: overseas, outside Great Britain and specified territories` EQUALS `the weekly rate immediately before the start of that part of the deferral period`
#ASSERT `regulation 23(4): the rate that stands in place of the weekly rate in regulation 12A(2)` `part: not an overseas resident` EQUALS `the weekly rate immediately before the end of that part of the deferral period`
-- (5): the increase or decrease is added to, or subtracted from, the regulation 22 amount.
#ASSERT `regulation 23(5): the increment where regulations 12A and 22 both apply` 10 2 EQUALS 12
#ASSERT `regulation 23(5): the increment where regulations 12A and 22 both apply` 10 (0 MINUS 3) EQUALS 7
#ASSERT `regulation 23(5): the increment where regulations 12A and 22 both apply` 10 0 EQUALS 10
